WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.602 --> 00:00:12.225
The waveform shows amplitude over time, but it does not say which frequencies are present. This sweep rises from 100 hertz to 10 kilohertz in four seconds.

2
00:00:16.971 --> 00:00:21.276
The spectrum shows which frequencies are in a block of time, but not when they appear.

3
00:00:21.977 --> 00:00:30.935
The spectrogram shows both: time on the horizontal axis, frequency on the vertical axis and intensity as color. The sweep appears as a rising line.

4
00:00:31.629 --> 00:00:43.613
An octave is double the frequency. Octave bands have centers at 125, 250, 500 hertz, 1, 2, 4 and 8 kilohertz, and their width grows with frequency.
